<title>USA: Conversion files merger-related offering.</title>
<headline>Conversion files merger-related offering.</headline>
<dateline>HAZLET, N.J. 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Conversion Technologies International Inc said on Friday it filed a registration statement to issue up to 850,000 common stock shares in conjunction with its previously announced merger with Octagon Inc.</p>
<p>The merger is to be completed in the first quarter of 1997 pending the approval of Octagon shareholders, who are to receive one Conversion Technologies share for every 10 Octagon shares. Octagon would become a wholly owned subsidiary of Conversion Technologies.</p>
<p>Octagon's net income for the 12 months ending last June 30 was $599,544 on revenues of $28.3 million. For the same period Conversion reported a net loss of $4.6 million on revenues of $2.7 million.</p>
</text>
